    "created_at": "2026-09-30T17:08:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T17:08:59Z",
    "body": "So as far as I understand this:\r\n\r\n> selectors could match an element before its parent in tree order when it becomes connected.\r\n\r\nWas introduced to avoid potential surprises because `<style>` under some element may give an impression that it'll only match elements under it, which I think is a good reason to discourage people from doing this.\r\n\r\n... Maybe we should require implicit `@scope`, which would apply selectors to only under the parent of the `<style>` element it's defined in? Seems that'd achieve the similar/same result with less work.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
