    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T17:35:25Z",
    "body": "@dshin-moz it's an option but would not allow using `@scope (selector)` or `@scope (selector) to (selector)`, which could exclude some use cases. Or if we do allow it, it needs selector matching anyway.\r\n\r\nEdit: actually `@scope` and `@scope to (selector)` can be allowed without needing selector matching since `to` can only limit the scope, not expand it.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
