    "created_at": "2026-09-30T17:54:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-30T17:54:59Z",
    "body": "I changed this to require `@scope` without a scope start (so the scoping root is the parent), as @dshin-moz suggested. The top level can otherwise only have `@namespace`, `@layer` statements, and `@media`/`@supports`/`@container`/`@starting-style`/`@layer` blocks that themselves follow this rule. So `@import` and at-rules with global effects like `@font-face`, `@keyframes`, and `@property` are out. This means conformance checkers no longer need to work out what selectors match or might match.\r\n\r\nI think the previous approach didn't work: \"could, at any time, match\" disallows most selectors, since script can mutate the DOM arbitrarily later on.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/5916747339/reactions",
      "total_count": 1,
