    "created_at": "2026-10-01T15:20:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T15:20:46Z",
    "body": "> at-rules with global effects like `@font-face`, `@keyframes`, and `@property` are out.\r\n\r\nIs this OK for the use cases? It's limiting what CSS features can be used, so potentially an annoyance and overly restrictive.\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n\r\n1. Keep it restrictive.\r\n2. All at-rules except `@import` are allowed despite global effects.\r\n3. As above but with a strong encouragement (non-normative) to only use the defined fonts, keyframes, etc. within the `style` element's parent.",
